.TH LINUX-DEVICE-MANAGER 1 "2026" "Linux Device Manager" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
linux-device-manager \- view and manage hardware devices on Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B linux-device-manager
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Linux Device Manager is a GTK4 application that enumerates devices from
sysfs/udev and displays them in a category tree with detail tabs (general,
advanced, driver, logs). Supported devices can be enabled or disabled through
a privileged helper governed by polkit; authentication may be requested.
.PP
The application bundles its own Java runtime under
.I /opt/linux-device-manager/runtime
and prefers it over the system Java.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /opt/linux-device-manager/
Application payload: Java libraries and the bundled runtime.
.TP
.I /usr/libexec/ldm-helper
Privileged device helper (executed via polkit).
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.ldm.policy
Polkit policy governing device enable/disable actions.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR lspci (8),
.BR lsusb (8),
.BR modinfo (8),
.BR udevadm (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Linux Device Manager contributors (https://github.com/getldm/linux-device-manager)
